# Token Efficiency

## Shell — prefix with `rtk`

`rtk` compresses command output (~60–90% token savings). Already installed; VS Code auto-approves it.

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| `git status` | `rtk git status` |
| `git log` | `rtk git log -10` |
| `git diff` | `rtk git diff` |
| `python -m pytest lib/tests/ -v` | `rtk python -m pytest lib/tests/ -q` |
| `python -m lib.cli.app list --json` | `rtk python -m lib.cli.app list --json` |

Add output limits (`-q`, `--co`, `-10`, `--tb=short`) even with rtk. Use `rtk proxy <cmd>` only when full raw output is required.

Meta: `rtk gain` (savings dashboard), `rtk discover` (missed opportunities).

## Monitor savings

Run `rtk gain` periodically (weekly or after heavy agent sessions). High-impact
commands in this repo: `git diff`, `git log`, `pytest`, `sfa ... --json`.
Use `rtk discover` to find commands still running without the prefix.

## Context discipline

- **Navigate via index** — use `.claude/PROJECT_INDEX.md` (hub) + `PROJECT_INDEX_MODULES.md` (tables on demand); don't re-scan the tree.
- **Read selectively** — large files (e.g. `lib/dash/integrated_dashboard.py`) with offset/limit; grep before full read.
- **Cite, don't paste** — reference code as `startLine:endLine:path`; never dump whole files in replies.
- **Scoped rules load on demand** — signals/dash/sfa-cli rules apply only when editing matching paths.
